263	  /* R6 §3, two stacked causes, both fixed here:
264	     1) .showcase-side's natural content (all 5/6 rows, R5's rise-mask kept
265	        every body visible at once) was taller than the embed cell's
266	        explicit height. A CSS grid item with an explicit height does not
267	        stretch to match a taller sibling's row track - the TRACK grows to
268	        fit the tall side instead, leaving the embed cell short of the
269	        row's actual height by the difference (measured ~110px), exposing
270	        the stage's own black gap background below the frame. Pinning both
271	        columns to the SAME explicit height (with the side's own
272	        overflow-y:auto as a never-clip safety net) makes them structurally
273	        impossible to mismatch, regardless of how much text a future edit
274	        adds.
275	     2) That explicit height was `100svh - 48px`, sized to sit BELOW the
276	        48px sticky topline - but the pin (`start:'top top'`) puts the
277	        section's rendered top at the viewport's own y:0, with the topline
278	        merely painted on top of (not offsetting) its first 48px. The
279	        result: content correctly avoids the topline visually, but then
280	        runs 48px short of the viewport's bottom edge, showing the stage's
281	        black background as a trailing band under both columns (measured:
282	        embed/side bottom at 852 of a 900-tall viewport). Hero's own pin
283	        has this identical 48px arithmetic and gap - invisible there only
284	        because it lands on the page's own black background either side.
285	        Showcase's is visible because there's real content flush above it.
286	        Fixed the same way hero's is invisible: fill the FULL viewport
287	        (100svh) - the topline still visually covers the top 48px (it's
288	        position:sticky, z-index:40, opaque), but the bottom now lands
289	        exactly on the viewport edge, so no gap is left to expose.
290	
291	     R7 runda 2, fynd 1: that "topline merely painted on top" claim was
292	     wrong for `.showcase-head`'s own rubrik - the topline IS opaque and
293	     DOES cover whatever renders in its first 48px; it just happened not to
294	     matter for hero (dark ground either side). Here `.showcase-head`'s
295	     headline-40 sits flush at the pinned section's very top edge, so its
296	     cap-height rendered UNDER the topline and got visually sheared (lead's
297	     through-05..through-12, 2026-09-25). Fix: pin the section 48px lower
